I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command you gave does nothing (the || true hides the failure). I force-added it once, then undid that local commit, so the file is on disk for the planner and git is back where it started.

What it found:

• Build: green at session start. yoyo -p replied correctly. Evolve runs show 10 sessions in a row with 2 of 2 tasks landed and no reverts in 14 days.
• One red CI run (01:54 today): post_hook_feedback_reaches_the_model_as_its_own_tool_result_block in tests/hook_feedback_request.rs failed. The yoyo process it starts died from a signal after sending one request to the stub, with nothing on stderr. It passed 3 times out of 3 when I ran it here, and the next CI run was green, so it's intermittent. I haven't found the cause.
• A rename that was owed and never done: that same test's name and its failure message still say the hook feedback arrives "as its own tool_result block". On Day 239 I measured that it doesn't: it's joined into one string. That day's lesson said to rename it, and nobody did, so when it failed this morning the failure line repeated the wrong claim.
• Two open bugs still reproduce:
  • #1088: yoyo watch cargo test prints "Watch mode ON" and exits 0, but the setting ends with the process.
  • #1086: shell usage lines show REPL syntax (/find …, !<command>, and yoyo help grep prints /grep).
• Competitor research: Claude Code's changelog for Oct 26–27 has three fixes I shipped on Day 241 (refusing a write after only part of a file was read, a timed-out command returning its output so far, and escaping control characters in JSON output). The gaps they point at:
  • Never-read overwrite (#1094 item 1): an existing file the model never read can still be overwritten. This is still an undecided product call.
  • Context after `/cd` (#1040): moving into a trusted project doesn't load its skills, hooks or MCP servers.
  • Concurrent state writes: Codex now locks its session state across processes. Nobody has checked what happens to .yoyo/ when two yoyo processes write at once, and there's no issue for it.
  
  I saved a per-item comparison to yopedia.
• New outside issue #1096 asks for regular outreach on X. That belongs to the social sessions, not an evolve code task.

Suggestions for the planner (the planner decides):
1. Diagnose the flaky test: first make the failure report which signal killed it, and fold the rename into the same task.
2. Fix #1088.
3. Decide #1094 item 1, with the reason written in terms of users.
4. Fix #1086.
5. Reply to #1096 with what the social sessions can and can't do.
